@startuml
' Card selection modes -- synchronous vs. asynchronous (informative)

' == THEME ==

skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
skinparam activity {
    ' Activity
    BorderThickness 2
    ' Default (no stereotype) => Yellow
    BackgroundColor #FEFECE
    BorderColor #D4AC0D
    ' Stereotype <<blue>> => Blue
    BackgroundColor<<blue>> #EBF5FB
    BorderColor<<blue>> #3498DB
    hide <<blue>> stereotype
    ' Order is very important! Diamond styling must be last,
    ' otherwise it will override the default activity style.
    ' Diamond => Red
    DiamondBackgroundColor #FDEDEC
    DiamondBorderColor #E74C3C
    DiamondBorderThickness 2
}

' == CONTENT ==

|Application|
start
:**prepareSelection()**
build the card selection scenario; <<blue>>
if (selection mode?) then (synchronous)
  :**processCardSelectionScenario()**
  or
  **processMultichannelCardSelectionScenario()**; <<blue>>
  |Card reader|
  :execute the scenario
  on the already-present card;
  |Application|
  :receive **CardSelectionResult**;
  :process the card;
  stop
else (asynchronous)
  :**scheduleCardSelectionScenario()**; <<blue>>
  :**startCardDetection()**; <<blue>>
  |Card reader|
  :wait for a card, then execute
  the scheduled scenario on insertion;
  :notify **CardReaderEvent**
  **CARD_MATCHED** / **CARD_INSERTED**
  (per **CardPresenceNotificationPolicy**);
  |Event handler|
  :**parseScheduledCardSelectionsResponse()**; <<blue>>
  :process the card;
  :**endCardProcessing()**; <<blue>>
  stop
endif
@enduml
